==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|denoter}}, from {{der|en|la|denotare}}, from {{m|la|de-||complete}} and {{m|la|notare||to mark out}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈnəʊt/|a=RP}}
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈnoʊt/|a=GA}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-denote.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|əʊt|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To indicate; to [[mark]].
#: {{ux|en|The yellow blazes '''denote''' the trail.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To make [[overt]]. {{rfex|en}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To refer to [[literally]]; to convey as [[objective]] [[meaning]].
#: {{cot|en|connote|evoke|allude}}
#: {{ux|en|The prefix {{m|en|pre-}} '''denotes''' "before", as in {{m|en|preview}}.}}

====Derived terms====
